    <h2>Explanation</h2>
    <div class="group-desc">
        <p dir="ltr">You will be shown a series of maps. On each map,<b> </b>there are three routes to move from point 1 to point 2. Sometimes, there is also information shown about rockfall. You should rank the routes according to your preference.&nbsp;</p>

<p dir="ltr">There are no right or wrong answers. Each map will be shown individually, and you will not be able to return to previous maps.</p>

<p dir="ltr"><b id="docs-internal-guid-e54448fa-7fff-7829-07bf-8c101b79779c">Keep in mind this information when you are answering the questions:</b></p>

<p dir="ltr"><b id="docs-internal-guid-e54448fa-7fff-7829-07bf-8c101b79779c">Weather: </b>You are hiking on a spring day in the Alps. Weather conditions are stable and identical across all routes. Any influence of weather on rockfall occurrence is already reflected in the hazard information shown on the map.</p>

<p dir="ltr"><b id="docs-internal-guid-e54448fa-7fff-7829-07bf-8c101b79779c">What is rockfall: </b>Rockfall is the rapid detachment and downslope movement of rock blocks. In this study, all rockfalls are considered large enough to cause injuries to humans or damage to the trail.</p>

<p dir="ltr"><b id="docs-internal-guid-e54448fa-7fff-7829-07bf-8c101b79779c">We will start with a practice round, without rockfall information.</b></p>

